#### Eigenvalues:

- $E_1 = K$ (from $|00\rangle$)
- $E_4 = K$ (from $|11\rangle$)
- The middle 2×2 block:
$$
H_{\text{mid}} = \begin{pmatrix}
-K + 2\Delta & 2J \\
2J & -K - 2\Delta \\
\end{pmatrix}
$$

Let us denote this as:
$$
H_{\text{mid}} = \begin{pmatrix}
a & b \\
b & c \\
\end{pmatrix},\quad a = -K + 2\Delta,\quad c = -K - 2\Delta,\quad b = 2J
$$

Eigenvalues:

$$
E_{\pm} = \frac{a + c}{2} \pm \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{(a - c)^2 + 4b^2}
= \frac{-2K}{2} \pm \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{(4\Delta)^2 + 4(2J)^2}
= -K \pm \sqrt{4\Delta^2 + 4J^2}
= -K \pm 2\sqrt{J^2 + \Delta^2}
$$

So the full spectrum is:

$$
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
E^{(1)} &= K \quad &\text{(from } |00\rangle) \\
E^{(2)} &= K \quad &\text{(from } |11\rangle) \\
E^{(3)} &= -K + 2\sqrt{J^2 + \Delta^2} \\
E^{(4)} &= -K - 2\sqrt{J^2 + \Delta^2}
\end{aligned}
}
$$

But wait: $E^{(3)}$ and $E^{(4)}$ come from the middle block. Let us order them properly.

Set:
$$
\omega = \sqrt{J^2 + \Delta^2}
$$

Then the two middle eigenvalues are:
$$
E_+ = -K + 2\omega,\quad E_- = -K - 2\omega
$$

So the full spectrum is:

$$
\boxed{
\text{Spectrum of } H: \quad K \ (\text{twice}),\quad -K + 2\sqrt{J^2 + \Delta^2},\quad -K - 2\sqrt{J^2 + \Delta^2}
